# ─── Auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is the credential the SPAWNED Claude Code CLI uses — the server itself has no
# login and no accounts. Per turn it uses the FIRST available, in this order:
#   1. the caller's own key sent in a request header (BYOK section below)
#   2. a server ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set here
#   3. the Claude subscription token (CLAUDE_TOKEN) set here
# Set whichever fallback you want — either or both; if both are set the API key wins
# over the subscription.

# Claude subscription (Max/Pro). Generate with `claude setup-token`; the server maps it
# to CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN (the var the CLI reads).
#CLAUDE_TOKEN=sk-ant-oat01-your-token-here

# Anthropic API key. If set, it takes precedence over CLAUDE_TOKEN above.
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-api03-your-key-here

# ─── Per-request BYOK (bring-your-own-key) ───────────────────────────────────
# Optional. A caller can send an Anthropic key in a request header and the server reads
# it fresh per request and injects it into the spawned CLI for that turn only (never
# stored). Useful when the key should not live in this file:
#   claude mcp add --transport http --scope user likeminds <url> \
#       --header "x-api-key: sk-ant-api03-YOURKEY"

# Header the key is read from (default x-api-key; also accepts Authorization: Bearer).
#LIKEMINDS_MCP_KEY_HEADER=x-api-key

# ─── Optional overrides ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Model for spawned turns. Default is opus[1m] (latest Opus, 1M-token context).
# If an API key lacks 1M-context Opus access, use a model it can serve, e.g. sonnet.
#CLAUDE_AGENT_MODEL=opus[1m]

# Path to the claude CLI (default: resolved from PATH).
#CLAUDE_BIN=/usr/local/bin/claude

# Where the server listens. Loopback by default — the server is unauthenticated, so
# only bind it wider behind something that does the access control for you.
#LIKEMINDS_MCP_HOST=127.0.0.1
#LIKEMINDS_MCP_PORT=8787

# Per-turn and wait-for-user-reply timeouts, in seconds.
#LIKEMINDS_MCP_TURN_TIMEOUT=1800
#LIKEMINDS_MCP_REPLY_TIMEOUT=3600

# ─── Host-path access (Docker only) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# `input_paths` is resolved INSIDE the container, so host paths need a bind mount to be
# visible. docker-compose.yml mounts this directory read-only at /host and the server
# rewrites paths under it, which is what lets you pass any local path unchanged.
#
# DEFAULT: your whole home directory ($HOME). That is broad — the spawned CLI runs with
# permissions bypassed, so everything under it is readable, including ~/.ssh, ~/.aws and
# other projects' .env files. Narrow it to the smallest directory holding your source
# material; paths outside whatever you set here stop resolving, and the server says so
# rather than starting a run with missing files.
#LIKEMINDS_HOST_MOUNT=/Users/you/Downloads

# ─── Global skill kill-switch ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hide skills so they can be neither listed nor run. Edit disabled_skills.json
# ({"disabled": ["skill-name"]}) at the project root — read fresh per call, no restart.
# This env var is an optional comma-separated override, merged with that file.
#LIKEMINDS_MCP_DISABLED_SKILLS=skill-a,skill-b
#LIKEMINDS_MCP_DISABLED_SKILLS_FILE=disabled_skills.json
